Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DSH_PACKAGE@ (>= @DSH_MIN_VERSION@)
Recommends: gh, git
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Homepage: @PLUGIN_REPO_URL@
X-DSH-Plugin-Name: @PLUGIN_NAME@
X-DSH-Plugin-Version: @PLUGIN_VERSION@
X-DSH-Plugin-Commit: @PLUGIN_COMMIT@
Description: /code-review command for DeepSeek Harness
 Adds the /code-review slash command and the prepare_code_review tool to
 DeepSeek Harness. The command starts a structured review of a GitHub pull
 request in a background subagent: the child reads the pull request metadata,
 per-file patches, and complete files at the head commit, then reports
 evidence-backed findings.
 .
 On the Web client, the plugin's page in Plugins carries a settings card for
 the report language, finding limit, and context budgets.
 .
 Installs the plugin package root under @PLUGIN_INSTALL_DIR@.
 It does not modify any user profile. Enable it for a profile with:
 .
   dsh plugin --profile @PROFILE@ add @PLUGIN_INSTALL_DIR@
 .
 or add the same directory on the Plugins page in the Web UI.
 .
 Reviewing a pull request needs the GitHub CLI (gh) signed in. The plugin is
 architecture-independent JavaScript and runs inside the Harness Host process
 with the profile user's privileges.
